A||N||15||V8Dreamer||fuel injector isn't injecting :(||||1||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||11-11-2001||09:56 PM||||Well, my 86 2m4 won't start....I figured it was a problem with the distributor(I washed the engine, the distributor always a problem after that) but, as it looks now, it's not getting any fuel.  I had my roommate crank it over and it is definitely not getting any fuel.  I checked the fuel filter to see if it was possibly blocked somehow, but it was not, and the fuel pump is working fine (my roommate turned the key on while I had the filter off...a series of woah woah woah followed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  I checked both the red and blue wires and both have 12v to ground when the key is on.  what else can I check to isolate the problem??  I don't know much about fuel injection, so ANY help would be great!  Thanks a lot in advance...<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||11-11-2001||10:15 PM||||Check the fuel injector fuse and the ECM fuse. Both of then are 10 amp fuses I think.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake_Dragon||11-11-2001||10:39 PM||||Check your fuel pressure with a gauge, my pump would shoot gas out of the line but if I would have checked it with a gauge it would have saved me $100.<BR>Turned out to be the small hose going from the pump to the hard line in the fuel tank, had a small slit in it that would open when the pump came on.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||roadwarrior||11-11-2001||10:49 PM||||you better hope that your injector didn't seize up on you, I don't know if it's a common problem or not, but if you need one I've got one.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Dreamer||11-12-2001||12:07 AM||||I knew I forgot something....I did check the fuses.....thanks for the suggestion though...<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000005||V8Dreamer||11-12-2001||02:04 PM||||I looked over all of the fuel lines and I didn't find any problems anywhere.....does anyone know what else I could test to isolate the problem to the injector itself and not a wiring problem??  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||jelly2m8||11-12-2001||04:27 PM||||If you have fuel pressure and the wiring looks ok, check to see if you have spark at the plugs, or coil.<P> If you don't have either, replace the pickup coil in the distributer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||V8Dreamer||11-12-2001||04:39 PM||||I haven't checked for spark yet, but I am positive that there isn't any fuel being injected, so regardless of whether I have spark, I still have to fix the fuel problem before it will start..... thanks for the suggestion anyway though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ryan||||reg||7
Z||000008||88formula||11-12-2001||05:37 PM||||Check the ignition pickup coil in the distributor! No signal no fuel injector pulse from computer. <P>You'll need a DVM and a manual for that. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||V8Dreamer||11-12-2001||07:58 PM||||formula88:  Thanks a lot man, I'll check that out tomorrow afternoon...after a quick run to AZ.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fierowrecker||11-12-2001||08:07 PM||||Hey Ryan!<BR>I had the same thing happen...<BR>I even checked codes, got #12, but no gas...<BR>Finally swapped ECM, and it fired right up...<BR>The ECM output chip took a dump and wouldn't fire the injector...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000011||V8Dreamer||11-13-2001||11:23 AM||||Fierowrecker:<BR>Thanks for the input.....that's another thing I was kinda wondering about....I think I'm gonna see if I can grab a spare ECM from Rockcrawl today and possibly plug that in today before I begin rebuilding the distributor.......thankfully, my GT is running pretty well, so I don't have to rush to get the coupe fixed, I just like to have them both running so I have one to fall back on.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000012||ITB 2M4||11-13-2001||01:10 PM||||I just replaced the fuel pump in mine not to long ago.  I bought a new fuel injector and put it in cause I figured the old one was on it's last legs.  After putting the new one in, the car wouldn't run.  I put the old one back in, and after a few tries, the car fired right up.  A couple of mechanic friends suggested getting the fuel pressure tested.  It was about half as much as the lowest factory acceptable rating.  So I replaced the fuel pump, and it works like a charm now.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000013||V8Dreamer||11-13-2001||08:19 PM||||Well, I got ahold of a spare ECM and that didn't change anything..... I guess I'm gonna have to rebuild the distributor next.....anyone else have any other suggestions?<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000014||V8Dreamer||11-16-2001||02:22 PM||||SHE LIVES!!!!!!!  <BR>Well, I replaced the ign mod and vrooooom (really more like cough cough, rattle rattle, but it doesn't help to dream right?)  Anyway, I'm not sure whether it was indeed the ign mod or the pickup coil since I had to wrestle with the coil to get it to let go of the module.....and the pickup coil is from Autozone.  So, tomorrow I'm just going to rebuild the distributor (new p-up coil and new module) as a bit of preventative maintenance.  Just thought I'd let all of you guys who made suggestions know what the resolution was.  Thanks Formula!<P>Ryan||||reg||14
Z||000015||V8Dreamer||11-16-2001||03:36 PM||||Oh, and one more thing.....in my midst of What the hell is wrong with this thing's.....I had swapped the ECM out with another one from an 86 2.5 manual (same as mine) and when I started er up, it idled around 3,000 RPM, so it really was like vrooooooom!  After I drove it for about a block bucking and carrying on, I bumped my elbow on the second ECM and remembered that I had swapped them......I shut her off, put the original back in and voila, instant normal idle.  thanks again everyone for your suggestions, I REALLY appreciated it.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
